   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `python -m fieldnotes.cli export`. It prints one line per note as `DATE: TEXT`, for example `2026-01-02: first`. The project checks pass: 2 tests ran and the line-length rule found nothing.\n\n- **Date format:** `DATE` is the date part only (`YYYY-MM-DD`), taken from the note's `created` timestamp. If you'd rather have the full timestamp, change `[:10]` in `fieldnotes/cli.py` to nothing.\n- **Usage message:** it now reads `add TEXT | list | export`.\n- **Test:** the new test is in `tests/test_cli.py`. It adds two notes and checks the exact output lines.\n- **Running the checks:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set, so I ran it with a temporary directory: `NOTES_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" python tools/check.py`.",
